==Evolution==
Evolves into '''Jellycat''' at level 10.

Evolves into '''Jelly Dumpling Cat''' when obtained from [[Be Bee Queen (Merciless)]] (guaranteed to drop) and is level 20 or above.

==Strategy/Usage==
Because of his extremely low HP (even lower than [[Nerd Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Cyberpunk Cat]] at the same level), as well as his long attack rate, he should be used as a suicide bomber dealing massive burst damage for taking out mildly strong peons and also for chipping down/knocking back backliners with his wave. He's very useful in [[Bakoo]], [[King Wahwah]], and [[Everlord Wanwan]]'s stages as his wave attack gives him significant reach, with enough damage to force them back. Albeit more rare to see, Slime Cat may miss his attacks when attacking enemies that have been recently knock backed.  Overall, this unit is very powerful, but requires special attention to not die instantly.

Slime Cat is also fairly effective in stages with [[:Category:Zombie Enemies|Zombies]], since they may un-burrow in front of Slime Cat and become a stepping stone for a Wave Attack, though do note its lack of [[Zombie Killer]]. Frontline enemies with Single Attack or slow attack speed are also fairly easy to use as stepping stones. Slime works well against LD enemies with a sizable blindspot (such as [[Dolphina]], [[Henry]], and [[Tackey]]), given that it has an above-average speed.

This Cat works well with Cats who can freeze enemies, as well as with [[Freshman Cat Jobs (Super Rare Cat)|Headmaster Cat Jobs]] and, of course, the Thunderbolt cannon. Time Slime to hit an enemy whose offensive power is temporarily nullified and you can use him against almost anything.

Along with this, Slime Cat can be used to make a frame perfect trade with [[Aku Doge]], allowing both it and the Doge to die at the same time. This can be used to buy more time for money before hitting the base.

==='''True Form'''===
The most important buffs Jelly Dumpling Cat receives are a range increase from 140 to 180 and a speed increase from 15 to 20. This alone allows Jelly Dumpling Cat to far more reliably attack instead of faltering to fierce frontliners. Instead of falling to a boosted [[Doge Dark]] or [[Gabriel]], it can simply generate a wave off them. The range increase is also enough to ensure he outranges most if not all melee enemies, such as [[Gory]] and the majority of his variants, [[Shy Boy]], [[Boraphim]], etc. The increased speed also allows Jelly Dumpling Cat to sneak into blind spots of Long Distance enemies more reliably, with the exception of [[Golem Sunfish]], who they no longer fit into the blind spot of. Timing and skill are still needed to make use of this unit, but these attacks are now far more consistent.

Additionally, the wave level increase from 5 to 7 allows Jelly Dumpling Cat to strike even more of the field. In the aforementioned Zombie stages, the extra range can make even better use of reviving and unburrowing enemies as stepping stones. The extra range also allows him to hit [[Raynard]] much easier than before.

Although somewhat inconsistent (one of the sides has a chance to kill the other early without taking damage, unlike in the case of Aku Doges where success is guaranteed), Jelly Dumpling Cat can now do a frame perfect trade with a lot more enemies. Enemies such as [[Sir Rel]], [[Relic Doge]], [[Mr. Angel]], [[Doge Dark]], and [[Wild Doge]] can trade with Jelly Dumpling Cat if you wish to stall in the beginning or simply want to get rid of multiple threats.

